## Returning Objects
Functions can create and return objects:

```ts
function createUser(name: string, age: number) {
    return {
        name: name,
        age: age,
        isAdmin: false
    };
}

const user = createUser("Steve", 25);
console.log(user.name);  // Steve
```

### Shorthand
When the property name matches the variable name, you can shorten it:
```ts
function createUser(name: string, age: number) {
    return { name, age, isAdmin: false };
}
```

Same result, less typing.


